.TH CLRU_DECLARE_SCOPED 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clru_declare_scoped \- declare an LRU cache that is destroyed at scope exit
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clrucache.h>

clru_declare_scoped(name, KeyT, ValT);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Does what clru_declare() does, and also attaches
__attribute__((cleanup(___clrucache_destroy))) to the variable, so the
compiler destroys the cache automatically when the variable leaves its
scope. Call clru_init() on the variable before you use the cache.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name  Variable name for the cache handle
KeyT  Key type
ValT  Value type
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
This macro needs GCC or Clang, because it uses __attribute__((cleanup)).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clru_declare (3),
.BR clru_construct_scoped (3)
